# REGRESSION PIN — `newtype` over `Option[int]`, the cell that was ACCIDENTALLY
# GREEN TWICE OVER (Core #12 / SIX-Q #6).
#
# WRONG BEFORE THE FIX (measured at pristine HEAD): `gg build` rc 1 on both
# backends — the payload registered as `_0: Unit`.
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE EXISTS IN THIS SHAPE BECAUSE ITS FIRST TWO SPELLINGS DID NOT
# PIN ANYTHING:
#   • Asserting `"built"` made it green under the registration-half-only
#     compiler, which returns `none` for `Some(5)` — a LOUD BUILD FAILURE traded
#     for a SILENT WRONG ANSWER, and the fixture could not see it.
#   • `Option[int]` gets no drop glue, so the bad store the emitted C carried
#     was harmless: the cell was green for a reason unrelated to what it claimed
#     to test.
# Reading the payload back through `is Some(x)` is what makes it a pin. Measured
# with the STRUCTINIT HALF REVERTED: C builds rc 0 and prints `none` for
# `Some(5)`, deterministically. Do not weaken this assertion.
newtype NO(Option[int])

void main():
    Option[int] o = Some(5)
    NO a = NO(o)
    if a.0 is Some(x):
        print(x)
    else:
        print("none")
